# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository.
#
# This is not a style preference. A shell script or a Dockerfile checked in
# with CRLF fails inside a container with an error that names neither the file
# nor the reason — the shebang line ends in an invisible carriage return and
# the interpreter is reported as not found.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Binary files must not be normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Lockfiles are generated. Marking them keeps a dependency bump from burying
# the change it accompanies under thousands of lines a reviewer will scroll
# past — and scroll past the real diff with it.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
